# pkg(8) manifest template. build-pkg.sh expands the version placeholder below
# and writes the result to the metadata directory as +MANIFEST. Do not repeat
# that placeholder in a comment: the substitution is a plain sed and would
# rewrite it here too. pkg fills in the ABI
# (e.g. FreeBSD:14:amd64) from the host it is built on, which is why we build
# one package per supported FreeBSD release.
name: cloudbackup
version: "${PKG_VERSION}"
origin: sysutils/cloudbackup
comment: "Server/client backup tool with cloud blob store support"
maintainer: alexandru@ionica.eu
www: https://github.com/aionica/cloudbackup
prefix: /usr/local
categories: [sysutils]
desc: <<EOD
CloudBackup - server/client backup tool with cloud blob store support
(AWS S3, Azure Blob Storage, GCP Storage). Runs as a daemon exposing a
REST API; ships with a CLI client for on-demand operations.
EOD
